# =============================================================================
# The enquiry endpoint — /api/enquiry
#
# COPY TO .env.local FOR LOCAL WORK, AND SET THE REAL VALUES IN THE HOST'S
# ENVIRONMENT (Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables) FOR
# PRODUCTION. Never commit a filled-in copy: .env.local is gitignored, this
# file is not, and nothing in here may ever carry a real password.
# =============================================================================

# --- Where enquiries go ------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults to info@topcatworktops.co.uk when unset. Set it only to divert a
# staging deployment somewhere harmless. A request can never change it.
# ENQUIRY_TO=info@topcatworktops.co.uk


# --- 1. SMTP: the real path --------------------------------------------------
# With these set, the site composes and sends the email itself and depends on
# nothing else. Either give SMTP_URL, or the host/user/pass trio.
#
# SMTP_URL=smtps://website%40topcatworktops.co.uk:PASSWORD@mail.example.com:465
#
# SMTP_HOST=mail.topcatworktops.co.uk
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=website@topcatworktops.co.uk
# SMTP_PASS=
# SMTP_SECURE=            # optional; defaults to true on port 465, false on 587
#
# The address the email is FROM. It must be one the SMTP account is allowed to
# send as — not the visitor, who is the Reply-To instead. Defaults to SMTP_USER.
# SMTP_FROM=Topcat Worktops website <website@topcatworktops.co.uk>


# --- 2. The legacy endpoint: the fallback ------------------------------------
# While SMTP is unset, the route hands the same multipart to the old site's
# send.php, which is still live and still mails info@topcatworktops.co.uk.
# Defaults to the URL below when unset.
#
# ⚠️ THIS POINTS AT THE OLD HOST. When the new site goes live on the real
# domain, either configure SMTP above (preferred) or repoint this at the
# production host's own /send.php. If that host is ever retired with SMTP still
# unset, enquiries stop being delivered — and the visitor is correctly told so
# with a 502, but nobody wants to find out that way.
# ENQUIRY_FORWARD_URL=https://thadeusg3.sg-host.com/send.php

# Set it to an empty string to turn delivery off entirely for local work, so
# the forms can be developed without mailing anyone:
# ENQUIRY_FORWARD_URL=
